<title>USA: Lucas Aerospace gets Lockheed unit contract.</title>
<headline>Lucas Aerospace gets Lockheed unit contract.</headline>
<dateline>AURORA, Ohio 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>LucasVarity Plc said Tuesday its Lucas Aerospace unit has been awarded a contract from Lockheed Martin Corp to design and manufacture a system which provides emergency back-up power for modified demonstrator F-16 aircraft.</p>
<p>The contract value for the emergency power generating system for the Joint/Integrated subsystems technology demonstrator program was not disclosed.</p>
<p>LucasVarity is a global automotive, diesel engine, aftermarket and aerospace group.</p>
